# C++ style for csrc/. Enforced by pre-commit so it is not a thing anyone has to remember.
#
# Three settings are the operator's explicit requests and are written down so clang-format
# enforces them instead of them being re-litigated in review:
#
#   NamespaceIndentation: All      the body of a `namespace X {` is indented (V45; ledger A3).
#                                  LLVM's default is `None`, which is why the first version of
#                                  csrc/ was flat.
#   IndentWidth: 4                 four spaces, as the Python side (V44; ledger A1).
#   AccessModifierOffset: -2       `public:` half-outdented, members one level deeper.
#
# ColumnLimit matches the Python side (black's line-length 96), so a file does not change shape
# depending on which language it is written in. That decision predates this file's rewrite and
# was lost in it; restored.
---
Language: Cpp
BasedOnStyle: Google
Standard: c++17
ColumnLimit: 96
IndentWidth: 4
AccessModifierOffset: -2
NamespaceIndentation: All
IndentPPDirectives: BeforeHash
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: Inline
DerivePointerAlignment: false
